{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:6213c5468b52afb3","name":"Skull Squadron Pilot","source":{"id":"source:reference-6213c5468b52afb3","title":"Skull Squadron Pilot","revision":20310,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T23:36:43Z","sha256":"a39cb145bb2f36d377d1268dcfbe3396836c521c3b022488b43fd495b00e0d26","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=20310","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Skull%20Squadron%20Pilot&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-6213c5468b52afb3","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Legacy Era Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Legacy_Era_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skull Squadron"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skull_Squadron","referenceId":"reference:fe211a0fc3bc10c7"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Empire","referenceId":"reference:f9c9a48674cc3415"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The pilots of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skull Squadron"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skull_Squadron","referenceId":"reference:fe211a0fc3bc10c7"}," are among the most dedicated pilots in the galaxy. Skull Squadron's mission- the defense of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Coruscant"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Coruscant","referenceId":"reference:2ee37a21e9e7a955"}," and all of its Imperial assets- keeps their skills honed, as they must maintain the security of one of the most heavily populated worlds in the galaxy. The pilots of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skull Squadron"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skull_Squadron","referenceId":"reference:fe211a0fc3bc10c7"}," are handpicked for service by the squadron's commander and serve for as long as they are able to demonstrate their superior piloting skills. Though slip-ups usually result in pilot deaths, a few pilots have lived long enough to retire from ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skull Squadron"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skull_Squadron","referenceId":"reference:fe211a0fc3bc10c7"}," and go on to greater things, including Moff ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rulf Yage"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rulf_Yage","referenceId":"reference:e14e4fbb0185ff43"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Though primarily a planetary defense force, the pilots of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skull Squadron"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skull_Squadron","referenceId":"reference:fe211a0fc3bc10c7"}," are no strangers to engagements above other worlds and in the depths of space. However, Skull Squadron Pilots spend countless hours performing maneuvers and training above ",{"tag":"a","children":["Coruscant"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Coruscant","referenceId":"reference:2ee37a21e9e7a955"},", learning to fly and fight between the towering skyscrapers found across the planet. A pilot in ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skull Squadron"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skull_Squadron","referenceId":"reference:fe211a0fc3bc10c7"}," must learn to maneuver between artificial structures, dodge ",{"tag":"a","children":["Airspeeders"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Airspeeders","referenceId":"reference:8831ac17fd67f6fc"}," and incoming space traffic, and still pinpoint and destroy their prey. Flying in an urban environment can be extremely challenging, and that is why the members of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skull Squadron"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skull_Squadron","referenceId":"reference:fe211a0fc3bc10c7"}," must have the quickest reflexes and the sharpest instincts.\n"]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Skull Squadron Pilot Statistics (CL 8)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Human"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Human","referenceId":"reference:9ffa865f2bc6e850"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Soldier"],"href":"https://swse.mir